Description: Use MAJOR-only SOVERSION for the shared library
 The upstream CMake sets SOVERSION to "MAJOR.MINOR", which makes the
 shared-library SONAME change on every minor release.  Under Debian's
 binary-package naming convention (libfoo<SOVERSION>) that would force
 the package to be renamed (libduckdb1.4 -> libduckdb1.5 -> ...) at
 every upstream minor release, which is unhelpful for downstream users
 tracking a PPA.
 .
 This patch reduces SOVERSION to MAJOR only.  Reverse dependencies
 will still be pinned via dh_makeshlibs / dh_shlibdeps against the
 real upstream version recorded in the SONAME, so cross-minor
 incompatibility surfaces at install time even though the package
 name does not change.
 .
 Independent reimplementation; not derived from any third-party
 patch.  The rationale is the standard Debian library-packaging
 convention documented in Debian Policy section 8 and the Debian
 Library Packaging Guide.
Author: Michal J. Gajda <mjgajda@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-05-17

--- a/src/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -107,7 +107,7 @@ link_threads(duckdb PUBLIC)
 if(SET_DUCKDB_LIBRARY_VERSION)
   set_target_properties(
     duckdb PROPERTIES VERSION ${DUCKDB_VERSION_NUMBER}
-                      SOVERSION ${DUCKDB_MAJOR_VERSION}.${DUCKDB_MINOR_VERSION})
+                      SOVERSION ${DUCKDB_MAJOR_VERSION})

 endif()

